<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narrative of a Five Years Expedition against the Revolted Negroes of Surinam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1796</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Stedman's Narrative</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Narrative of a Five Years Expedition against the Revolted Negroes of Surinam is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-gabriel-stedman">John Gabriel Stedman</a>'s account of his service against the maroons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> from 1773 to 1777, published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1796. Illustrated with engravings by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-blake">William Blake</a> and others, it described the brutality of plantation <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> as well as the landscape and peoples of the colony, and it was widely read in the debate over abolition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narrative-of-a-five-years-expedition.jpg" alt="Narrative of a Five Years Expedition against the Revolted Negroes of Surinam" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Gabriel Stedman / Francesco Bartolozzi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bartolozzi_-_John_Gabriel_Stedman_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
